# Local halo — faithful port of `chamonix-viirs-2025.html`

The prototype is the visual and technical reference. Do not reinterpret it.

## Locked baseline

- Precomputed 3D field 96×48×96 RG half float (R occluded, G unoccluded), ±12 km, 0.3–8.3 km at Chamonix
- Emitters = every positive native VIIRS pixel centred in the zone, at relief + 20 m, weight = radiance × area / 10
- Screening: 360 samples per voxel/emitter, precomputed in a worker, cached by `haloFieldCacheKey`
- Screen pass: depth-stopped ray march, 112 jittered steps, prototype density / opacity / tint formulas
- Halo keeps the prototype curve `(1 − exp(−1.5c))^(1/2.2)`; the scene keeps its sRGB output
- `src/__tests__/localHaloField.test.ts` must keep matching the embedded prototype volume

## Forbidden

| Hack | Why |
|---|---|
| Hemispheres, balls, veils, sprites, PointLights, horizon gradients, emissive terrain paint | Not the prototype's volume |
| Invented cities, per-city normalisation, radiance thresholds, colours read back from maps | Must come from the native raster |
| Running the 360-sample screening per pixel or per frame | Sliders only update uniforms |
| Global exposure / tone-mapping changes to make the halo look right | Fix the halo instead |
| Mesh raycasts for the hover probe | Height-field samples only |

## Rule of landing

Halos off and VIIRS diagnostic off → the frame must take the untouched `direct` path.
